  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.346,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you remember this pattern from Grade 6? The picture below explains why each subsequent inverted L gives the next odd number:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.157,
            0.359,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.168,
                0.157,
                0.359,
                0.215
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.171,
                0.223,
                0.221,
                0.24
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "1 + 3"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.141,
            0.646,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.41,
                0.141,
                0.646,
                0.217
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.256,
                0.222,
                0.385,
                0.24
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "1 + 3 + (3 + 2)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.41,
                0.223,
                0.492,
                0.24
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "1 + 3 + 5"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.527,
                0.223,
                0.689,
                0.241
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "1 + 3 + 5 + (5 + 2)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.712,
            0.141,
            0.812,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.712,
                0.141,
                0.812,
                0.216
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.707,
                0.223,
                0.823,
                0.24
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "1 + 3 + 5 + 7"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.253,
            0.846,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that the sum of the first n odd numbers is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { 2 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Alternatively, every square is a sum of successive odd numbers starting from 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.307,
            0.192,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.307,
                0.192,
                0.374
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.318,
            0.826,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In mathematics, sometimes arguments and reasoning can be presented without any words. Visual proofs can be complete by themselves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.4,
            0.848,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also, we can find out whether a number is a perfect square by successively subtracting odd numbers. Consider the number 25, successively subtract 1, 3, 5, ... until you get or cross over 0,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.475,
            0.29,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "25 – 1 = 24"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.324,
            0.475,
            0.427,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "24 – 3 = 21"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.463,
            0.475,
            0.569,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "21 – 5 = 16"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.604,
            0.475,
            0.696,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "16 – 7 = 9"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.73,
            0.475,
            0.814,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9 – 9 = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.51,
            0.846,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This means 25 = 1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 9 and is thus a perfect square. Since we subtracted the first five odd numbers, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 5 = 5 ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.558,
            0.683,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the pattern above, find 362, given that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 5 ^ { 2 }   =   1 2 2 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.583,
            0.847,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From the question we know that 1225 is the sum of the first 35 odd numbers. To find 36"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", we need to add the 36th odd number to 1225."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.623,
            0.531,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How do we find the 36th odd number?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.648,
            0.847,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The 1st odd number is 1, 2nd odd number is 3, 3rd number is 5, …, 6th odd number is 11 and so on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.689,
            0.43,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " odd number?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.714,
            0.424,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " odd number is 2n–1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.733,
            0.522,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the 36th odd number is 71."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.751,
            0.609,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By adding 71 to 1225, we get 1296, which is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 6 ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.77,
            0.847,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider a number such as 38 that is not a square and subtract consecutive odd numbers starting from 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.819,
            0.304,
            0.838
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "38 – 1 = 37"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.332,
            0.819,
            0.437,
            0.838
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_30.jpg",
          "content": "37 - 3 = 34"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 31,
          "bbox": [
            0.584,
            0.82,
            0.689,
            0.838
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "29 – 7 = 22"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 32,
          "bbox": [
            0.711,
            0.819,
            0.816,
            0.838
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "22 – 9 = 13"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 33,
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.849,
            0.304,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13 – 11 = 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 34,
          "bbox": [
            0.331,
            0.849,
            0.451,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2 – 13 = – 11"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 35,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.879,
            0.847,
            0.918
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This shows that 38 cannot be expressed as a sum of consecutive odd numbers starting with 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 36,
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
            0.916,
            0.112,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 37,
